experiment: wordruler
  SHORT RUN — 150000 ticks against a minimum of 450000. derived: §51's own estimator could not see what its teacher aimed at --
  axis_sep = 1.0 is the gap between two echo postures 2 Hz apart on F1, so
  worth +0.0008 of a formant separation. §52 re-asks the question on the
  FORMANT gap. The budget is a QUARTER of §51's and that is a power
  argument, not thrift: the paired SD GROWS with ticks (0.0451 at 150k ->
  0.1689 at 450k) because bias_ctx_ is a clamped accumulator whose slots
  random-walk apart, so more ticks buy NEGATIVE power. Projected to 1.8M the
  2 SE bar would be 0.225, which would not even detect §51's own +0.1889.
  Run at 450k AND 900k as a pre-registered dose axis, because one budget is
  itself a selection when the SD moves with it. Six arms: T1.ORACLE rises to
  n=36 (it was the load-bearing NULL in §51) and gains T1.ORACLE.D, the arm
  without which ORACLE's gap cannot be told from what a pinned two-slot
  table does alone. Clause 3 prints the RULER FIRST. kRead: every branch,
  the four VOIDs included, prints a reading rather than returning false
  Everything below is printed for debugging and is NOT a
  measurement; this run cannot pass whatever it reads.

  the question      §52. §51's primary could not see what its teacher aimed
                    at: axis_sep = 1.0 is worth +0.0008 of a formant gap. Same
                    question, scored on the quantity a listener hears.
  what §51 left     T1.ORACLE read +0.1889 on the formant gap -- 236x the
                    echo-posture ceiling -- with NO SE and NO decorrelated
                    twin, so it could not be separated from what a pinned
                    two-slot table does by itself. T1.ORACLE.D is that twin.
  the budget        chosen on POWER, not outcome: the paired SD GROWS with
                    ticks (0.0451 at 150k -> 0.1689 at 450k), so more ticks buy
                    NEGATIVE power here. Two budgets run as a dose axis.
  session           150.0 s of simulated life x 168 sessions, 6 arms
  instrument        wordruler   trial seed 0000000001357569   168 sessions
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)

  CLAUSE 3 (FIRST, DELIBERATELY) -- THE RULER. §51 discovered AFTER spending
  its budget that axis_sep = 1.0 is the gap between two echo postures that are
  THE SAME VOWEL. `echo gap` is what full compliance is worth in formant terms.
    the gap AVAILABLE between the two words is 1.6417 (a voice exactly on one
    word scores perr(the other)), so every `echo gap` below is read against it.
    T0.RET       |axis|^2 in F1+F2 0.1909   echo gap +0.0008 = 0.05% of available   <-- NOT A FORMANT RULER
    T1.RET       |axis|^2 in F1+F2 0.2008   echo gap -0.0228 = 1.39% of available   <-- NOT A FORMANT RULER
    T1.RET.D     |axis|^2 in F1+F2 0.2008   echo gap -0.0228 = 1.39% of available   <-- NOT A FORMANT RULER
    T1.ORACLE    |axis|^2 in F1+F2 0.2008   echo gap -0.0228 = 1.39% of available   <-- NOT A FORMANT RULER
    T1.ORACLE.D  |axis|^2 in F1+F2 0.2008   echo gap -0.0228 = 1.39% of available   <-- NOT A FORMANT RULER
    T1.BASE      |axis|^2 in F1+F2 0.1717   echo gap +0.0057 = 0.35% of available   <-- NOT A FORMANT RULER
    CONFIRMED: axis_sep is reported below as a SECONDARY ONLY and no verdict
    rests on it. This is §51's correction applied before the fact.

