  THE PRIMARY -- THE FORMANT GAP at the silent probe: perr(the OTHER word)
  minus perr(ITS OWN word), so positive means the voice sits closer to the word
  this object is named by. The units a listener hears.
    T0.RET       formant gap +0.0127 +- 0.0098  (n 12, 7 > 0)   [axis_sep +0.0583 +- 0.0306]   §50's teacher -- the rung on axis_sep, predicted NULL/NEGATIVE on formants
    T1.RET       formant gap -0.0002 +- 0.0073  (n 36, 17 > 0)   [axis_sep -0.0065 +- 0.0293]   THE CLAIM
    T1.RET.D     formant gap -0.0064 +- 0.0052  (n 36, 17 > 0)   [axis_sep -0.0158 +- 0.0245]   word DRAWN -- the primary's control
    T1.ORACLE    formant gap +0.0819 +- 0.0177  (n 36, 27 > 0)   [axis_sep +0.0698 +- 0.1429]   perfect index -- the CEILING
    T1.ORACLE.D  formant gap -0.0220 +- 0.0203  (n 36, 15 > 0)   [axis_sep -0.0381 +- 0.1166]   perfect index, word DRAWN -- THE ARM §51 LACKED
    T1.BASE      formant gap -0.0024 +- 0.0068  (n 12, 5 > 0)   [axis_sep +0.0159 +- 0.0476]   table OFF -- the association route

  CLAUSE 4 -- THE RUNG: does the protocol teach AT ALL? T0.RET on axis_sep
  +0.0583 +- 0.0306 = 1.9 SE above zero: FAIL. (§51 read +0.5295 at 1.8M and +0.0583
  at 150k, so the MAGNITUDE is budget-dependent and is NOT the bar -- a 2 SE
  test asks what the rung means.) On the FORMANT primary §51 measured T0 at
  -0.0059, so T0 is predicted NULL OR NEGATIVE here and reads +0.0127 +- 0.0098;
  a LARGE POSITIVE T0 would contradict §51's ruler calibration.

  CLAUSE 5 -- THE VERDICT. Paired by creature, bar 2 SE, sign unconstrained.
    T1.RET - T1.RET.D         +0.0062  (paired SE 0.0075, 0.8 SE)   <-- PRIMARY
    T1.ORACLE - T1.ORACLE.D   +0.1039  (paired SE 0.0284, 3.7 SE)   <-- CEILING

    (1) VOID: T0 did not reproduce §50's effect on its own ruler. The refusal is the result.
